## How to read it

A transcript is read only through cc-transcript, by the path above, in pages. Never search `~/.claude` recursively.

```sh
cc-transcript show <path> --signal --width 300 --range A:B
cc-transcript show <path> --errors --all --width 300
cc-transcript permissions <path>
cc-transcript tools <path>
cc-transcript grep '<pattern>' <path> --max-matches 50 --timeout-ms 5000
```

The first number `show` prints on a line is that event's index. Cite it.

Records: run each query above and page forward by replacing its `--since` with `'#<last seq printed>'`. `cci show '#N'` prints one record whole. Cite the seq.

A log is read in line ranges with the Read tool. Cite the line number.

## The findings file

Write `{{.Findings}}`, appending each claim the moment you have confirmed it, so a compaction loses nothing. Group claims under `##` headings by theme. Every line that starts with `- ` is one claim in plain words, saying what happened, where and how often, and it ends with its cites:

```
- The hook refused the same push three times before the lane changed the command. [#362766] [#362790]
- The lane retried the install after each timeout, four in a row. [68531111-afa1.jsonl:4120] [supervisor.log:88]
```

`[#N]` is a record seq and `[<file name>:<n>]` is a transcript event index or a log line. A claim you cannot cite stays out. Say what you saw; causes and fixes belong to the triage. If the corpus holds no answer, write one claim saying so, citing the first and last thing you read.

## Finish

```sh
{{.Binary}} bulk triage {{.JobPath}}
```

It refuses a claim with no cite, or a cite outside the corpus, naming each line: fix those lines and run it again. It launches {{.Triage}} on Opus and prints the runner's verdict. If it refuses because no orca runner is alive, ignore its advice to spawn an Agent: arm a Monitor on `cci watch --drive {{.Drive}} --lane desk-runner --kind state --topic orca`, and at its first line run the step again. Then:

```sh
cci post --lane {{.Reader}} --drive {{.Drive}} --kind done --to {{.Triage}} "findings in {{.Findings}}"
```

and send the preamble's `worker_done`. Your caller already has the findings path, so report to nobody else. Anything that stops you goes to {{.Launcher}} as `--kind blocker`.
